          '**Structured Opioid Taper Protocol**:\n\n**General Principles**:\n- **Slow and steady**: For patients on long-term opioids (>1 year), taper by **5-10% of the total daily dose every 2-4 weeks**\n- **Patient-centered**: Adjust pace based on tolerance. This is NOT a race.\n- Her prior failures were from **50% abrupt reductions** — far too aggressive\n- At 120 mg MED, a 10% reduction = 12 mg decrease every 2-4 weeks\n\n**Sample Taper Schedule** (starting from morphine ER 60 mg BID + IR 15 mg TID PRN = ~165 mg/day):\n\n**Phase 1 (Weeks 1-8): Eliminate PRN doses**\n- Week 1-2: Reduce IR morphine from 15 mg QID PRN to 15 mg TID\n- Week 3-4: Reduce to 15 mg BID\n- Week 5-6: Reduce to 15 mg daily\n- Week 7-8: Discontinue IR morphine entirely\n- Now at 120 mg/day (morphine ER 60 mg BID only)\n\n**Phase 2 (Weeks 9-24+): Taper ER formulation**\n- Reduce by 10-15 mg every 2-4 weeks:\n- Weeks 9-10: Morphine ER 60 mg AM + 45 mg PM (105 mg)\n- Weeks 11-12: 45 mg BID (90 mg)\n- Weeks 13-14: 45 mg AM + 30 mg PM (75 mg)\n- Weeks 15-16: 30 mg BID (60 mg)\n- Weeks 17-18: 30 mg AM + 15 mg PM (45 mg)\n- Weeks 19-20: 15 mg BID (30 mg)\n- Weeks 21-22: 15 mg daily (15 mg)\n- Weeks 23-24: 15 mg every other day, then discontinue\n\n**Total taper duration: approximately 6 months** (appropriate for 5 years of use)\n\n**Withdrawal Symptom Management**:\n| **Symptom** | **Management** |\n|---|---|\n| Anxiety, irritability | Hydroxyzine 25 mg PRN; optimize buspirone/duloxetine |\n| Insomnia | Trazodone dose increase; melatonin 3-5 mg; sleep hygiene |\n| GI symptoms (nausea, diarrhea, cramping) | Loperamide, ondansetron, dicyclomine |\n| Myalgias, arthralgias | NSAIDs (ibuprofen 400 mg TID), warm baths, gentle stretching |\n| Diaphoresis, rhinorrhea | Clonidine 0.1 mg BID (also helps anxiety and autonomic symptoms) |\n| Pain flare | Reassurance that temporary flare is expected; non-opioid analgesics; do NOT increase opioid dose |\n\n**Monitoring During Taper**:\n- Clinic visits every 2-4 weeks during active taper\n- PEG scale at each visit to track pain and function\n- PHQ-9 and GAD-7 monthly (monitor for worsening depression/anxiety)\n- UDS periodically to confirm adherence\n- PDMP check at each visit\n- Celebrate milestones — positive reinforcement of progress',
